 "notes": "Blender Z up, faces -Y, left = +X, metres; all bone rolls 0. root and saddle do not deform. saddle head sits on the back surface (z 1.88) behind the withers, between the wing roots: the rider hips go there. socket_offsets loc are armature-space metres relative to the bone head (head offset = middle of the skull). Legs: leg_*_01 = shoulder point->elbow (front) / hip->stifle (hind), _02 forearm / gaskin, _03 cannon, hoof_* fetlock->ground. Wings rest raised and folded back; the arm (wing_*_01) points up from a broad root on the shoulder, so a flap is mostly a rotation about armature X+Y at wing_*_01 (see docs/notes/rig_pegasus.md for tested glide/down/up angles). feather_01 = secondaries (child of wing_02), feather_02 = lower primaries (child of wing_02), feather_03 = mid primaries (child of wing_03); keep relative fan/curl rotations within ~20 deg: neighbouring feathers are fused in the mesh. Mane rides neck_01..03/head; the rear mane behind rest y -0.6 (lying on the withers) rides neck_01 + spine_03 only, and the back behind the wing roots (y > -0.30, where the rider sits) has no neck weight, so neck moves do not move the saddle area. The fused mane/wing-root and wing-lobe/flank contacts are blended, not ripped (a rip opens see-through holes); the hanging feather lobe rides the wing. Breastplate rides spine_03. Tail hair rides tail_01..05/hips (5 bones). Keep neck_01/neck_02 within ~25/15 deg and tail lift within ~60 deg for clean skin."
}